    },
    {
      "@type": "HowTo",
      "@id": "#how-it-works",
      "name": "How simple-agent-collabs runs one research turn",
      "description": "Each researcher repeats these steps in parallel with the others. Jev makes the quick decisions; code checks citations; an LLM gives a second opinion only when Jev is unsure.",
      "tool": [
        {
          "@type": "HowToTool",
          "name": "goal.md"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToTool",
          "name": "board.md"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToTool",
          "name": "Jev (TypeSafe AI)"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToTool",
          "name": "GPT-6 researcher models"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToTool",
          "name": "GPT-6 Luna as second opinion"
        }
      ],
      "step": [
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "position": 1,
          "name": "Pick an open thread",
          "text": "The researcher reads the board and takes the first open thread or question. Jev checks it isn't already covered by another claim."
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "position": 2,
          "name": "Claim it",
          "text": "The claim is written to the board under a lock, so two researchers never take the same thread."
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "position": 3,
          "name": "Choose a model",
          "text": "Jev picks a tier: fast for lookups, standard for comparisons, powerful for recommendations."
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "position": 4,
          "name": "Research with tools",
          "text": "The LLM reads files, searches, and fetches pages with read-only tools. If the thread depends on unfinished work, it gives the thread back and posts a question."
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "position": 5,
          "name": "Check the citations",
          "text": "Code checks that every cited file, line, and page exists. A missing one is rejected without asking a model."
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "position": 6,
          "name": "Judge the claim",
          "text": "Jev reads the cited passages and gives the probability that they back the whole claim. Below 0.5 it is rejected; the researcher retries once with the reason."
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "position": 7,
          "name": "Second opinion",
          "text": "If Jev is unsure, below 0.8, an LLM reads the same passages, decides, and explains."
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "position": 8,
          "name": "Post the finding",
          "text": "The finding is appended to the board. After each round, Jev estimates whether the goal is answered and the run stops above 0.85."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "@id": "#question",
      "name": "Is Jev a better gate for research findings than an LLM-as-judge, and what question phrasing makes Jev's gate reliable?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Jev on its own is not proven better than an LLM judge, but Jev first with an LLM second opinion beat either alone. Jev checks every finding against the fetched source text; when it is unsure, GPT-6 Luna decides. On 30 labeled findings it agreed with every label in one run, let no bad finding through, and cost $0.0012 for the set. One finding sat on the 0.5 cut-off, so the fair reading is 29 or 30 out of 30. The earlier gate, which showed Jev only the citation text, let 14 of 20 bad findings through.",
        "dateCreated": "2026-09-24"
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Dataset",
      "@id": "#eval",
      "name": "Finding-gate eval: 30 labeled research findings",
      "description": "10 correct findings and 20 bad ones (6 overreach, 5 wrong number, 3 contradicted, 3 unsupported, 3 fake citation), each citing frozen source files. Labels were written by Claude and have not been independently reviewed.",
      "dateCreated": "2026-09-24",
      "measurementTechnique": "Each judge rules pass or fail on every finding; agreement with the label, bad findings passed, cost, and time are recorded. Run 2026-09-24T07:09Z.",
      "variableMeasured": [
        {
          "@type": "PropertyValue",
          "name": "Old gate: Jev on citation text only: agreement with labels",
          "value": 14,
          "maxValue": 30
        },
        {
